  "query_preview": "..\n\nThe center of a broad area of surface high pressure will slowly \nshift over the Ohio Valley tonight into Tuesday, then push off to \nour east Wednesday. In addition, HREF probabilities of fog have \nincreased for late tonight. Have added fog to the grids based on this\ninformation. Otherwise, fair skies and light winds are expected.\n\nReturn flow around the high will offer a short period of above \nnormal temperatures starting Wednesday and continuing until a cold \nfront moves into the Ohio Valley on Friday. The front will produce a \nchance of showers and storms late Thursday and Friday.\n\nGuidance becomes less certain heading into the weekend. There remains\nsome evidence that additional shortwave activity could cause a wave\nto form and bring periods of showers Saturday into early Sunday.",
